    <tags>audio volume sound playback-device switcher hotkeys tray osd mpc-hc volume2</tags>
    <summary>Tray utility in the spirit of Volume²: switch the default playback device with F7/F8, change the volume with F2/F3 and an on-screen overlay.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
A Windows system tray utility in the spirit of [Volume²](https://github.com/irzyxa/Volume2).

## Features

- **F7/F8** switch the default playback device (console, multimedia and communications roles together); a notification shows the new device.
- **F2/F3** lower/raise the master volume by 2% with an on-screen volume overlay. The overlay also appears on volume changes from any other source.
- **F5** shows/hides an always-on-top overlay with MPC-HC playback progress (requires the MPC-HC web interface).
- **Ctrl+F2** turns all the other hotkeys off and back on (e.g. while gaming).
- Hotkeys fire only without modifiers: Alt+F4, Ctrl+F5 and the like reach applications as usual.
- The tray menu lists all active playback devices and has a "run at Windows sign-in" option.

The log and an optional `.env` configuration file live in `%LOCALAPPDATA%\volume_switch`.
]]></description>
  </metadata>
  <files>
